{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_ne_A_census","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_ne_A_census","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L85-L88","doc":"And the derived polynomial is **not** the census one as it stands: at `(L, M) = (2, 0)` the\nderived `A` is `8` and the census polynomial is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_census_eq_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_census_eq_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L78-L83","doc":"**The census `5_2` is the derived polynomial under `L ↦ L⁻¹`**: over a field, for `L ≠ 0`,\n`L³ · A(L⁻¹, M) = A_census(L, M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_census","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_census","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L73-L76","doc":"Culler's `A_{K3_2}`, transcribed from the held census tarball. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_involution","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L53-L59","doc":"The boundary-orientation involution: over a field, for `L, M ≠ 0`,\n`L³ M¹⁴ · A(L⁻¹, M⁻¹) = A(L, M)` — the symmetry every knot A-polynomial carries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_complete_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_complete_point","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The complete structure `(L, M) = (−1, 1)` lies on the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_at_M_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_at_M_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L45-L47","doc":"Likewise over `M = −1` (the other lift of the meridian eigenvalue). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_at_M_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A_at_M_one","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L41-L43","doc":"Over `M = 1` the curve has only the parabolic point `L = −1`, with multiplicity three. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.A","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoAPolynomialFromFareyWord.lean#L36-L39","doc":"The recovered A-polynomial of the derived 5₂ triangulation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}